<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <Version>1.1.0</Version>
    <PackageId>TokenGuard.Extensions.Anthropic</PackageId>
    <Title>TokenGuard.Extensions.Anthropic</Title>
    <Authors>Svetlozar Stoykov</Authors>
    <Company>Svetlozar Stoykov</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Svetlozar Stoykov</Copyright>
    <Description>Anthropic integration for TokenGuard on .NET 10. Converts prepared TokenGuard messages to Anthropic request parts and lets TokenGuard use Anthropic to summarize older history when context gets tight.</Description>
    <PackageTags>tokenguard;anthropic;claude;llm;ai;agents;context-management;token-budget;prompt-management;dotnet</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Requires TokenGuard.Core 1.1.0 and Anthropic 12.53.0 or later. The summarizer logs and traces through the logger factory configured on the conversation.

Known limits: the token counter, summarizer, summary formatter, and builder registration of a custom compaction strategy are closed to consumers; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas; the package targets net10.0 only.

Full details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
      <PackageReference Include="Anthropic" Version="12.53.0" />
    </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\TokenGuard.Core\TokenGuard.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
